2025-12-01 09:47:13,701 - agent.executor - INFO -     Tool result: [{"paper_id":"35871080","title":"Identification of fusions with potential clinical significance in melanoma.","authors":"Moran JMT; Le LP; Nardi V; Golas J; Farahani AA; Signorelli S; Onozato ML; Foreman RK; Duncan LM; Lawrence DP; Lennerz JK; Dias-Santagata D; Hoang MP","abstract":"Though uncommon in melanoma, gene fusions may have therapeutic implications. Next generation sequencing-based clinical assays, designed to detect relevant gene fusions, mutations, and copy number changes, were performed on 750 melanomas (375 primary and 375 metastases) at our institution from 2014-2021. These included 599 (80%) cutaneous, 38 (5%) acral, 11 (1.5%) anorectal, 23 (3%) sinonasal, 27 (3.6%) eye (uveal/ conjunctiva), 11 (1.5%) genital (vulva/penile), and 41 (5.5%) melanomas of unknown primary. Sixteen fusions (2%) were detected in samples from 16 patients: 12/599 (2%) cutaneous, 2/38 (5%) acral, 1/9 (11%) vulva, 1/23(4.3%) sinonasal; and 12/16 (75%) fusions were potentially targetable. We identif...
