 as a scaffold protein. RAS mutations occur in about 30% of all human cancers. Moreover, BRAF","doi":"10.1016/j.phrs.2018.08.013","published_date":"2018-01-01T00:00:00","pdf_url":"","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30118796/","source":"pubmed","updated_date":"2018-01-01T00:00:00","categories":"","keywords":"","citations":0,"references":"","extra":""}]
