- Cannabinol (CBN) inhibits melanogenesis without cytotoxicity in α-MSH–induced B16F10 cells. CBN reduces melanin and tyrosinase activity dose-dependently; downregulates MITF, TYR, TYRP1/2; selectively suppresses p38, JNK, and NF-κB phosphorylation (ERK unaffected). High-purity CBN derived from CBD. Promising skin-whitening candidate.

- BRAF inhibition increases TGFβ2 and stimulates metastasis in mice with endogenous BRAF (wild-type context), highlighting a pro-metastatic risk of BRAF inhibitors in certain settings (notably HCC), via elevated TGFβ2 production.

