- Rac1-driven MAPKi resistance in melanoma involves reduced BRAF/MEK dependence, activation of JNK/p38 pathways, and partial YAP/TAZ reliance; undifferentiated cells acquire dependency on FAK. Combining the RAF/MEK clamp avutometinib with the FAK inhibitor defactinib suppresses Rac1-driven melanoma growth, offering a strategy for resistant, advanced disease.

