- ARAF/BRAF/CRAF kinase characterization defines activity and inhibitor sensitivity across RAF isoforms, informing the use and development of RAF inhibitor classes for diverse RAF mutations.

- Rotenone from Pachyrhizus erosus seeds potently inhibits melanogenesis in B16F10 cells (8 nM, minimal cytotoxicity). Mechanism: mitochondrial ROS generation activates ERK, driving MITF degradation; NAC or ERK inhibition reverses effects. Highlights mitochondrial damage–ERK–MITF axis in pigmentation control.

