- Observations: GAPDH translocates to nuclei in mouse hearts under pressure overload and in cardiomyocytes from patients with dilated 
Tool `Paper Search:search_medrxiv` with Parameter {'query': 'melanoma BRAF class 2 class 3 clinical trial protocol', 'max_results': 15} on Paper Search succeeded. Result (summarized from 10912 tokens): - Evaluating large language models for predicting psychiatric acute readmissions from clinical notes of population-based EHR (PsyRoBERTa) — Denmark
  - Data/Model: First psychiatry-specialized LLM (RoBERTa-based) trained on ~44 million psychiatric-relevant clinical notes covering Eastern Denmark; benchmarked vs three public general/medical-domain LLMs and a logistic regression baseline.
  - Findings: Outperformed comparators for predicting acute psychiatric readmissions (AUC=0.74) and recognized psychiatric diagnoses (AUC=0.85). Captured features aligning with clinical practice. Highlights value of domain-specific pretraining, including for non-English clinical data. (doi:10.1101/2025.03.07.25323558)

- Inferring pathogen superspreading potential using early spatial spread patterns
  - Methods: Branching process with US inter-county mobility; negative binomial transmission with mean R0 and dispersion r (lower r = stronger superspreading). Graph neural network infers r from early spatial spread; robust to R0 heterogeneity and underreporting.
  - Results: Stronger superspreading slows early spatial invasion and increases between-trajectory variability. Early US COVID-19: strong superspreading pre-lockdown (r=0.50; 95% CI 0.23–1.20), weaker post-lockdown (r=1.3; 0.64–3.18). Provides a population-level approach to quantify superspreading. (doi:10.1101/2025.10.28.25338965)

- Impact of later trading hours for bars/clubs on alcohol-related harms in Scotland: controlled interrupted time series (CITS)
