Tool `NASA Data:get_coronal_mass_ejection` with Parameter {'start_date': '2025-11-27', 'end_date': '2025-12-01'} on NASA Data succeeded. Result (summarized from 1664 tokens): Summary of CME activity (31 total; 2025-11-27 to 2025-11-28)

Overall pattern
- Location/direction: Majority observed to the NE/NNE/E, with many sources on or beyond the NE limb (several likely far-sided). Multiple successive narrow outflows and filament-related eruptions in the NE quadrant.
- Instruments: SOHO LASCO C2/C3, STEREO A COR2, GOES CCOR-1; sources and context from GOES SUVI 284/304.
- Data coverage: Several scheduled real-time data gaps in SOHO LASCO; some events only partially captured or seen primarily in CCOR-1/STEREO A.
- Source behavior: Continued outflow and gradual opening field lines beyond the NE limb; a large filament spanning much of the NE quadrant (seen in SUVI 304) begins erupting as early as 2025-11-27T16:00Z and contributes to multiple CMEs later on 2025-11-27.
- Speeds in listed subset: ~267–685 km/s. Types reported: S and C (as provided in DONKI analyses).

