Tool `NASA Data:get_coronal_mass_ejection` with Parameter {'start_date': '2025-11-30', 'end_date': '2025-12-02'} on NASA Data succeeded. Result: Coronal Mass Ejections found: 4nnID: 2025-11-30T00:36:00-CME-001nStart Time: 2025-11-30T00:36ZnSource Location: N19E89nNote: CME observed to the E in GOES CCOR-1 and STEREO A COR2, partially in SOHO LASCO C2 before a downlink gap beginning at 2025-11-30T00:48Z and not in SOHO LASCO C3 due to a downlink gap beginning at 2025-11-30T00:06Z. The source is likely field line movement on/beyond the NE limb around 2025-11-30T00:10Z in GOES SUVI 171/195/284, associated with a long duration C8.0 flare (N19E89) observed in GOES SUVI 131.nLink: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/43134/-1n  Analyses:n    - Time: 2025-11-30T04:55Z, Speed: 803.0 km/s, Type: Cn  Related event IDs (first 5):n    2025-11-30T00:16:00-FLR-001n----------------------------------------nnID: 2025-11-30T11:12:00-CME-001nStart Time: 2025-11-30T11:12ZnSource Location: nNote: This CME is visible to the east in SOHO LASCO C2/C3 and GOES CCOR-1. This event is not observed in STEREO A COR2 imagery due to a data gap starting at 2025-11-30T10:23Z. The source is likely far-sided as there are no corresponding source signatures on the Earth-facing disk around the time of this event.nLink: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/43146/-1n  Analyses:n    - Time: 2025-11-30T22:25Z, Speed: 317.0 km/s, Type: Sn----------------------------------------nnID: 2025-11-30T22:15:00-CME-001nStart Time: 2025-11-30T22:15ZnSource Location: nNote: Narrow CME first seen to the NE by GOES CCOR-1 beginning at 2025-11-30T22:15Z. This CME is not visible in SOHO LASCO C2/C3 due to a data gap beginning at 2025-11-30T19:30Z, and is not visible in STEREO COR2 due to a data gap beginning at 2025-11-30T10:23Z. The source of this CME is minor field line brightening and movement seen along the East limb in GOES SUVI 195 beginning at approximately 2025-11-30T21:36Z.nLink: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/43150/-1n  Analyses:n    - Time: 2025-12-01T07:00Z, Speed: 355.0 km/s, Type: Sn----------------------------------------nnID: 2025-12-01T02:48:00-CME-001nStart Time: 2025-12-01T02:48ZnSource Location: N23E90nNote: Halo CME first seen to the NE by SOHO LASCO C2 beginning at 2025-12-01T02:48Z, as well as by SOHO LASCO C3, STEREO A COR and GOES CCOR-1 in later frames. The source of this event is an X1.9 class flare which peaked at 2025-12-01T02:49Z located at approximately N23E90. This flare is visible in GOES SUVI 131, along with wide field line opening seen in GOES SUVI 171, 195 and 284. Filament ejecta is also visible from this region in association with the flare in GOES SUVI 304.nLink: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/43155/-1n  Analyses:n    - Time: 2025-12-01T04:45Z, Speed: 1837.0 km/s, Type: On  Related event IDs (first 5):n    2025-12-01T02:27:00-FLR-001n----------------------------------------
