2025-12-01 10:29:29,169 - benchmark.runner - INFO - Below is a concise, data-backed shortlist of California national parks that are strong for hiking, especially when starting from Los Angeles. For each, I’ve included current NPS alerts (with dates), visitor center details, entrance fees, and distance from Los Angeles. Where live driving distances could not be retrieved due to API failures, I provide straight-line (great-circle) distances calculated from official NPS coordinates and note any official NPS mileage statements.

Key recommendations for late fall/winter from Los Angeles
- Best all-around now: Joshua Tree (good winter temps; relatively close; some localized flood closures)
- Great coastal/wildlife option: Channel Islands (mainland VC is close; islands require boat; a few island-specific closures)
- Warm desert with big scenery: Death Valley (check flood-related road closures)
- Giant sequoias: Sequoia & Kings Canyon (many winter closures at higher elevations)
- Iconic granite/valley scenery: Yosemite (key roads closed for winter; some trail work closures)
- Shoulder-season hiking with fewer storms: Pinnacles (watch weekend capacity)
- Farther from LA and more winter-limited: Lassen and Redwood

1) Joshua Tree National Park (JOTR)
- Current alerts (NPS):
  - Queen Valley Complex Closed (Bighorn Sheep Rd, Queen Valley Rd, O’dell Rd) — Park Closure — updated 2025-11-16
  - Oasis of Mara Trail Closed (flooding) — Park Closure — updated 2025-09-28
  - Inaccurate Third-Party Apps — Caution — updated 2024-03-11 — https://www.nps.gov/subjects/digital/nps-apps.htm
  - Source (alerts): https://www.nps.gov/jotr/index.htm (Alerts section)
- Weather (NPS): Winter days ~60°F, nights can be freezing; spring/fall highs ~85°F, lows ~50°F; summer often >100°F. Source: https://www.nps.gov/jotr/index.htm
- Entrance fees (NPS): Vehicle $30 (7 days); Motorcycle $25; Per Person $15; Annual JOTR Pass $55. Source: https://www.nps.gov/jotr/index.htm
- Visitor centers (NPS):
  - Black Rock Nature Center — 9800 Black Rock Canyon Rd, Yucca Valley, CA 92284; typical hours 8–11 AM & 12–4 PM daily (seasonal variation). Source: https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/visitorcenters.htm
  - Cottonwood Visitor Center — from I‑10 exit 168; daily 8:30 AM–4:00 PM. Source: same as above
- Distance from Los Angeles:
  - Straight-line to Black Rock Nature Center: ~106 miles (computed from NPS coordinates 34.073359, -116.390638 and Los Angeles 34.052235, -118.243683).
  - Driving: verify live conditions via your preferred maps app using the above addresses (I attempted API retrieval but it failed).

2) Channel Islands National Park (CHIS)
- Current alerts (NPS):
  - Santa Rosa Island beach/dune closures near China Camp/Cluster Point — Park Closure — updated 2024-02-22 — https://www.nps.gov/chis/planyourvisit/backcountry-beach-camping-on-santa-rosa-island.htm
  - Santa Barbara Island Dock Closed; landings on adjacent rocky ledge — Info — updated 2018-01-23 — https://www.nps.gov/chis/planyourvisit/conditions.htm
- Weather (NPS): Mediterranean; highs mid‑60s°F, lows low‑50s°F year‑round. Source: https://www.nps.gov/chis/planyourvisit/weather.htm
- Entrance fees: None listed by NPS. Islands accessed only by boat/plane. Source: https://www.nps.gov/chis/index.htm
- Visitor center (mainland, Ventura) — 1901 Spinnaker Dr, Ventura, CA 93001; open daily 8:30 AM–5:00 PM; phone 805‑658‑5730. Source: https://www.nps.gov/chis/planyourvisit/visitorcenters.htm
- Distance from Los Angeles:
  - NPS statement: ~70 miles north of Los Angeles to the Ventura Visitor Center. Source: same page above
  - Straight-line to the Visitor Center: ~60 miles (coordinates 34.248454, -119.266582 vs. Los Angeles 34.052235, -118.243683).
- Notes: To hike on the islands (e.g., Anacapa, Santa Cruz), reserve boats with the park concessioner (see NPS site for planning links). Check island-specific closures.

3) Death Valley National Park (DEVA)
- Current alerts (NPS):
  - Many roads closed due to flooding on 2025‑11‑18 — Park Closure — updated 2025‑11‑19 — https://www.nps.gov/deva/planyourvisit/conditions.htm
  - Panamint Springs gas pumps closed at night; 7:00 AM–9:30 PM only (24‑hr gas at Furnace Creek & Stovepipe Wells) — updated 2025‑01‑27
- Weather (NPS): Winter has cool days/chilly nights; spring is most popular; summer extremely hot. Source: https://www.nps.gov/deva/index.htm
- Entrance fees (NPS): Vehicle $30 (7 days); Motorcycle $25; Per Person $15; Annual Park Pass $55. Source: https://www.nps.gov/deva/index.htm
- Visitor center (NPS): Furnace Creek VC — Furnace Creek, CA 92328; daily, year‑round. Source: https://www.nps.gov/deva/index.htm
- Distance from Los Angeles:
  - Straight-line to Furnace Creek Visitor Center: ~184 miles (36.461796, -116.866673 vs. 34.052235, -118.243683).
  - Driving varies widely with the current road closures; check the NPS Conditions page above before committing to a route.

4) Sequoia & Kings Canyon National Parks (SEKI)
- Current alerts (NPS):
  - Winter seasonal road closures — Mineral King Rd; Hwy 180 between Grant Grove & Cedar Grove; Panoramic Point Rd — updated 2025‑11‑23 — https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/road-conditions.htm
  - A few small roads closed due to roadway damage (Middle Fork, Redwood Canyon, South Fork, Crystal Cave Rds) — updated 2025‑09‑11 — same link as above
- Weather (NPS): Big elevation range; winter snow in sequoia groves, rain in foothills; chains often required. Source: https://www.nps.gov/seki/index.htm
- Entrance fees (NPS): Vehicle $35 (valid 1–7 days for both Sequoia & Kings Canyon). Source: https://www.nps.gov/seki/index.htm
- Visitor center (NPS): Foothills Visitor Center — 47050 Generals Hwy, Three Rivers, CA 93271; typically 8:00 AM–5:00 PM daily; phone 559‑565‑3341. Source: https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/visitorcenters.htm
- Distance from Los Angeles:
  - Straight-line to Foothills Visitor Center: ~172 miles (36.491072, -118.825591 vs. 34.052235, -118.243683).
  - Winter driving can be significantly longer; check chains and closures via the road conditions link above.

5) Yosemite National Park (YOSE)
- Current alerts (NPS):
  - Tioga Rd (Hwy 120 through the park) and Glacier Point Rd temporarily closed due to snow — updated 2025‑11‑21 — https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/wroads.htm
  - Vernal and Nevada Falls trail closures (weekday blasting for John Muir Trail repairs). Only access to Vernal Fall footbridge and Clark Point; no access to tops of Vernal/Nevada Falls — updated 2025‑11‑26 (see Yosemite alerts via main site)
- Weather/Access (NPS): Most precipitation Oct–May; high-elevation roads close in winter; chains may be required. Source: https://www.nps.gov/yose/index.htm
- Entrance fees (NPS): Vehicle $35 (7 days). Source: same page
- Key contact: Road conditions line 209‑372‑0200 (then 1, 1). Source: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/wroads.htm
- Distance from Los Angeles:
  - Straight-line to park center coordinates: ~272 miles (37.848833, -119.557187 vs. 34.052235, -118.243683).
  - Expect significantly longer winter drive times; verify via live mapping to “Yosemite Valley Visitor Center” and cross-check the road conditions link above.

6) Pinnacles National Park (PINN)
- Current alerts (NPS):
  - High Crowds & Park Capacity (parking/area closures likely 8 AM–3 PM on weekends when full) — updated 2022‑01‑19 — https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/hours.htm
- Entrance fees (NPS): Vehicle $30 (7 days); Annual $55. Source: https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm
- Visitor centers (NPS):
  - Bear Gulch Nature Center (East side) — typically 9:00 AM–4:00 PM select days; phone (831) 389‑4486 x4235
  - West Pinnacles Visitor Contact Station — typically 9:00 AM–3:00 PM; may close seasonally
  - Park Store (campground) — 9:00 AM–4:00 PM daily
  - Source: https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/directions.htm and Visitor Centers listings
- Distance from Los Angeles:
  - Straight-line to Bear Gulch Nature Center area: ~236 miles (36.48136, -121.18081 vs. 34.052235, -118.243683).

7) Lassen Volcanic National Park (LAVO)
- Current alerts (NPS):
  - Lassen National Park Highway closed for winter (Hwy 89) — updated 2025‑11‑17
  - Some access roads impassible due to snow/mud — updated 2025‑11‑19
  - Source: https://www.nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/weather.htm
- Entrance fees (NPS): Vehicle $30 (7 days; winter discount $10). Source: https://www.nps.gov/lavo/index.htm
- Visitor center (NPS): Kohm Yah‑mah‑nee VC — 21820 Lassen NP Hwy, Mineral, CA 96063; typically 9:30 AM–4:30 PM daily. Source: https://www.nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/visitorcenters.htm
- Distance from Los Angeles:
  - Straight-line to Kohm Yah‑mah‑nee VC: ~476 miles (40.43778, -121.53384 vs. 34.052235, -118.243683).

8) Redwood National and State Parks (REDW)
- Current alerts (NPS/CA State Parks within the unit):
  - Newton B. Drury Scenic Parkway closed to vehicles Dec 1–3 (open to pedestrians/bikes) — updated 2025‑11‑24
  - Source: https://www.nps.gov/redw/index.htm (Alerts)
- Entrance fees: None listed for the park system (some state parks facilities may have fees). Source: same
- Visitor centers (NPS/CA SP): Crescent City Info Center; Hiouchi Visitor Center; others with seasonal hours. Source: https://www.nps.gov/redw/planyourvisit/visitorcenters.htm
- Distance from Los Angeles:
  - Straight-line to Crescent City Information Center: ~623 miles (41.75281, -124.19404 vs. 34.052235, -118.243683).

How these distances were determined
- Straight-line (great-circle) distances are computed from the official NPS coordinates listed above to Los Angeles (34.052235, -118.243683). Conversion used: 1 degree latitude ≈ 69 miles; 1 degree longitude ≈ 69 × cos(average latitude) miles; then Pythagorean approximation for regional scale. You can verify using any great-circle calculator with the NPS coordinates provided.
- For Channel Islands, NPS explicitly states the Ventura Visitor Center is about 70 miles north of Los Angeles (source: https://www.nps.gov/chis/planyourvisit/visitorcenters.htm).
- Live driving distances/times: Please verify with your preferred map app using the visitor center street addresses above. My attempts to fetch Google Maps driving distances during this session failed due to API errors, so I have not quoted unsourced drive-time numbers.

Quick pick guidance from Los Angeles (with sources)
- Fastest/closest with good winter hiking: Joshua Tree. Expect cool days, cold nights; check localized flood closures (NPS alerts dates above). Fees: $30/vehicle. Visitor centers/hours listed above. Source: https://www.nps.gov/jotr/index.htm
- Easiest quick visit without mountain snow: Channel Islands Visitor Center in Ventura (about 70 miles from LA per NPS). For island hikes, book boats; check island-specific closures. Source: https://www.nps.gov/chis/index.htm
- Warm desert vistas (check flood damage): Death Valley conditions page before you go; many roads impacted as of 2025‑11‑19. Fees: $30/vehicle. Source: https://www.nps.gov/deva/planyourvisit/conditions.htm
- Sequoias in winter: Lower-elevation foothill trails can be accessible; higher-elevation areas (Mineral King, Cedar Grove) closed; chains may be required. Fees: $35/vehicle. Source: https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/road-conditions.htm
- Yosemite in winter: Valley is open, but Tioga and Glacier Point Roads are closed; weekday trail closures near Vernal/Nevada Falls for JMT repairs. Fees: $35/vehicle. Road conditions line: 209‑372‑0200 (then 1, 1). Source: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/wroads.htm

If you tell me which park you’re leaning toward, I can:
- Map out specific trail options that are currently open (cross-referencing the latest NPS alerts).
- Provide the exact driving route and travel time from your LA starting point once we run a live check.
- Suggest the best visitor center to start from, parking considerations, and backup hikes in case of day-of closures.
