- Designation: National Park
- State: CA
- Website: https://www.nps.gov/yose/index.htm
- Description: Yosemite encompasses nearly 1,200 square miles of deep valleys, grand meadows, ancient giant sequoias, vast wilderness, and iconic granite shaped by glaciers. First protected in 1864, it’s best known for waterfalls, High Sierra tranquility, and diverse landscapes.

Location
- Coordinates: 37.84883288, -119.5571873
- Address: PO Box 577, Yosemite National Park, CA 95389

Weather
- Elevation: ~2,000 ft (600 m) to 13,000 ft (4,000 m)
- Precipitation: ~95% Oct–May; >75% Nov–Mar
- Snow: Most of the park snow-covered Nov–May; Yosemite Valley can be rainy or snowy during winter storms

Getting There
- Year-round vehicle access via Highways 41, 140, and 120 from the west
- Tioga Pass Entrance (Hwy 120 from the east): typically closed approx. Nov through late May or June
- Hetch Hetchy: open year-round but may close intermittently due to snow; day-use only (see hours)
- Note: GPS directions may be inaccurate; check official guidance
- Driving info: http://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/driving.htm

Operating Hours
- Yosemite National Park: Open 24 hours/day, 365 days/year
- Hetch Hetchy: Open sunrise to sunset for day visitors; road closed sunset to sunrise (except permitted backpackers)

Contacts
- Phone: 209/372-0200
