Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'seki'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2778 tokens): SUMMARIZED CONTENT:
- Name: Sequoia & Kings Canyon National Parks (SEKI)
- Designation: National Parks
- State: CA
- Website: https://www.nps.gov/seki/index.htm
- Overview: Massive mountains, rugged foothills, deep canyons, vast caverns, and the world’s largest trees. Explore to plan visits or learn about plants, animals, and threats they face. Ancient giant sequoias, though massive, are vulnerable.

Location
- Coordinates: 36.71277299, -118.587429
- Address: 47050 Generals Highway, Three Rivers, CA 93271

Weather
- Wide variation due to extreme elevation range.
- Summer: Comfortable in sequoia groves; hot, dry foothills; snow lingers on high passes into summer.
- Fall: Can feel like summer or winter.
- Winter: Snow in sequoia groves, rain in foothills; be prepared for tire chains.
- Spring: Great foothill hiking; snow begins melting at higher elevations.

Directions
- Highways: CA-180 from Fresno to Kings Canyon NP (continues 30 miles east to Cedar Grove); CA-198 from Visalia to Sequoia NP via Three Rivers.
- Inside parks: Highway 198 becomes the Generals Highway, connecting 198 to 180.
- Vehicle advisory: Over 22 feet should enter via Highway 180.
- Winter: Generals Highway between parks often closes; chains may be required.
- No east–west roads cross the parks.
- Directions info: http://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Operating Hours
- Open 24/7, year-round. Some roads close in winter due to snow; rare extreme weather may close park access roads.

Contacts
- Phone (Voice): 5595653341
- Fax: 5595653730
- Email: SEKI_information@nps.gov

