Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'jotr'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2037 tokens): Joshua Tree National Park (code: jotr)
- Designation: National Park; State: CA
- Official site: https://www.nps.gov/jotr/index.htm

Overview
- Where the Mojave and Colorado Deserts meet, featuring diverse plants/animals, strong winds/occasional torrential rain-shaped geology, dark night skies, rich cultural history, and surreal rock formations in southern California.

Weather
- Typically clear; <25% humidity.
- Spring/Fall: avg highs ~85°F (29°C), lows ~50°F (10°C).
- Winter: days ~60°F (15°C), freezing nights; occasional snow at higher elevations.
- Summer: very hot; days >100°F (38°C), nights often >75°F (24°C).

Getting There
- From I-10: Exit 117 to CA Hwy 62 (access West Entrance, North Entrance, Black Rock, Indian Cove).
- From I-10: Exit 168 for the South Entrance.
- Directions info: http://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Location
- Coordinates: 33.91418525, -115.8398125
- Address: 74485 National Park Drive, Twentynine Palms, CA 92277-3597

Contacts
- Phone (Voice): 760-367-5500
- Fax: 760-367-6392
- Email: jotr_info@nps.gov

Fees and Passes
- Entrance – Private Vehicle: $30.00 (7-day permit for passengers of a single, non-commercial vehicle).
- Entrance – Motorcycle: $25.00 (7-day permit per motorcycle).
- Entrance – Per Person: $15.00 (7-day fee per person on foot or bike).
- Annual Entrance – Park: $55.00 (valid 12 months; covers signee and accompanying passengers in one non-commercial vehicle; sold at entrance stations and visitor centers).

Operating Hours
- Park open 24/7/365.
- Visitation peaks in spring (wildflowers), increases in fall, lowest in summer heat.
- Some areas are day-use only. Visitor centers have separate hours.

Topics/Themes
- Archeology; Farming and Agriculture; Ranches; Industry; Mining; Native American Heritage; Westward Expansion; Homesteading; Animals; Birds; Tortoises and Turtles; Climate Change; Geology; Groundwater; Freshwater Springs; Night Sky; Trails; Unique Species; Endangered; Wilderness.

Activities
- Auto and ATV; Scenic Driving; Astronomy; Stargazing; Biking.
- Camping: Backcountry; Car/Front-country; Horse/Stock; Group.
- Climbing; Rock Climbing.
- Food/Picnicking.
- Guided Tours; Self-Guided Tours (Walking and Auto).
- Hiking: Backcountry; Front-country.
- Horse Trekking; Horseback Riding; Horse Camping.
- Junior Ranger Program.
- Wildlife Watching; Birdwatching.
- Museum Exhibits.
- Shopping; Bookstore/Park Store.

Images
- Sample highlights include Quail Springs at sunset; Hidden Valley hiker views; historic Keys Ranch (ranger-guided access); Lost Horse Valley Joshua trees and rock outcrops; Junior Ranger program; dramatic sunsets and night skies; Jumbo Rocks Campground landscapes. Image gallery available via the official site.
