Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'pinn'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2983 tokens): - Name: Pinnacles National Park (code: pinn)
- Designation: National Park; State: CA
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm
- Description: Volcanic eruptions ~23 million years ago created rocky spires, deep canyons, and diverse environments from chaparral and oak woodlands to cool canyon floors.
- Location: 36.49029208, -121.1813607; Address: 5000 East Entrance Road, Paicines, CA 95043
- Weather: Mediterranean climate. Summers hot (often >100°F); winters mild (highs in 60s). Inland location brings wider seasonal variation and large day–night temperature swings year-round.
- Directions: West entrance via Hwy 101 to Soledad, then Hwy 146. East entrance via Hwy 25 (from Hollister in the north; from King City via Bitter Water Rd G-13 in the south). Note: No through road between east and west entrances. Directions info: http://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/directions.htm
- Operating hours:
  - East Side Entrance: Open 24/7, year-round (including holidays).
  - West Side Entrance: Daily 7:30 AM–8:00 PM; one-lane, narrow, winding road; oversize vehicles should use east side. Access to Prewett Point, Balconies, and Juniper Canyon trails.
- Contacts:
  - Phone: 831-389-4486 (voice); Fax: 831-389-4288
  - Email: pinn_visitor_information@nps.gov (include visit dates/season if applicable; replies usually within one week). For volunteer opportunities/service projects: pinn_volunteer@nps.gov
- Entrance fees:
  - Entrance – Private Vehicle: $30.00 (valid 1–7 days; all occupants; East and West entrances)
  - Entrance – Motorcycle: $25.00 (valid 1–7 days; East and West)
  - Entrance – Per Person: $15.00 (on foot/bicycle; valid 1–7 days; East and West)
  - Entrance – Non-commercial Groups: $15.00 per person, up to maximums for comparable commercial capacities ($40 or $100). Exempt: age 15 and under, valid pass holders, and hired drivers transporting only.
  - Commercial Entrance – Sedan (1–6 seats): $30.00
  - Commercial Entrance – Van (7–15 seats): $40.00
  - Commercial Entrance – Mini-bus (16–25 seats): $40.00
  - Commercial Entrance – Motor Coach (26+ seats): $100.00
  - Entrance – Education/Academic Groups: $0.00 (may qualify for Educational Fee Waiver; otherwise see fees for large/commercial groups)
- Entrance passes:
  - Annual Entrance – Park: $55.00 (valid 12 months from purchase; covers signee and accompanying passengers in a single non-commercial vehicle; available at entrance stations)
- Activities: Astronomy, Stargazing, Biking, Road Biking, Camping (Car/Front Country, Group, RV), Caving, Climbing/Rock Climbing, Picnicking, Citizen Science, Volunteer Vacation, Hiking (Backcountry, Front-Country), Junior Ranger Program, Wildlife Watching, Birdwatching, Park Film, Shopping (Bookstore/Park Store, Gift Shop/Souvenirs)
- Topics: Architecture and Building; Archeology; Colonization and Settlement; Dams; Engineering; Enslavement; Explorers and Expeditions; Farming and Agriculture; Ranches; Great Depression; Hispanic American Heritage; Industry; Mining; Immigration; Latino American Heritage; Migrations; Military; US Army; Native American Heritage; Presidents; Religion and Spirituality; Missions; Schools and Education; Science, Technology and Innovation; Social Movements; Conservation Movement; Transportation; Bridges; Roads, Routes and Highways; Tunnels; Tragic Events; Catastrophic Fires; Floods; Wars and Conflicts; Spanish-American War; Cold War; Westward Expansion; Homesteading; The Gold Rush; Ancient Seas; Animals; Birds; Cats (wild); Fish; Tortoises and Turtles; Wolves; Caves, Caverns and Karst; Canyons and Canyonlands; Climate Change; Fire; Foothills, Plains and Valleys; Forests and Woodlands; Coniferous Forests; Deciduous Forests; Fossils and Paleontology; Geology; Mineral Deposits; Groundwater; Aquifers; Freshwater Springs; Grasslands; Meadows; Mountains; Natural Sounds; Night Sky; Astronomy; River and Riparian; Rock Landscapes and Features; Scenic Views; Thickets and Shrublands; Trails; Unique Species; Rare; Endangered; Volcanoes
Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'lavo'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 3193 tokens): - Name: Lassen Volcanic National Park (code: lavo)
- Designation: National Park; State: CA
- Website: https://www.nps.gov/lavo/index.htm
- Description: Home to steaming fumaroles, wildflower meadows, clear mountain lakes, and numerous volcanoes. Jagged peaks reflect an eruptive past; hot water continues to shape the land.

Location
- Coordinates: 40.49354575, -121.4075993
- Address: 38050 Highway 36 East, Park Headquarters, Mineral, CA 96063

Weather
- Highly variable year-round.
- January averages: high 40.4 °F (4.7 °C), low 20.8 °F (-6.2 °C).
- July averages: high 88.4 °F (31.3 °C), low 49.8 °F (9.9 °C).
- On average: 36.9 days ≥ 90 °F; 164 days ≤ 32 °F annually.

Getting There
- From I-5 (Redding): Hwy 44 east 48 miles to Hwy 89; Hwy 89 south 1 mile to north entrance.
- From I-5 (Red Bluff): Hwy 36 E 51 miles to Hwy 89; Hwy 89 north 6 miles to south entrance.
- Directions page: http://www.nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Contacts
- Phone: 530-595-6100 (Voice)
- Email: lavo_information@nps.gov

Operating Hours
- Entire park, all entrances: Open year-round, 24/7.
- Road access is limited approximately November–May due to snow.

Entrance Fees (valid up to 7 consecutive days unless noted)
- Private Vehicle: $30. Digital passes available on recreation.gov when stations unstaffed.
- Private Vehicle (winter discount): $10. Same validity and digital pass note.
- Motorcycle: $25; Winter: $10. Same validity/digital pass note.
- Per Person (on foot/bicycle or non-commercial organized group in a vehicle): $15; Winter: $10. Same validity/digital pass note.
- Education/Academic Groups: $0 with approved fee waiver submitted at least two weeks prior.
- Commercial Tours (valid up to 7 consecutive days for same group; fees based on total seating capacity; annual/lifetime passes not accepted):
  - Sedan: $25
  - Van: $50
  - Mini-bus: $60
  - Motor Coach: $150

Entrance Passes
- Annual Entrance – Park: $55. Valid for one year from month of purchase at Lassen Volcanic and Crater Lake National Parks, Whiskeytown National Recreation Area, and Lava Beds National Monument. Admits one vehicle and occupants, or one motorcycle and riders, or pass holder + 3 others on bicycle/foot.

Topics
