  - Nixpkgs branches (e.g., nixos-25.11, nixos-unstable): https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/branches
  - Package search per channel: https://search.nixos.org/packages (use the channel parameter)

Home Manager availability and option counts
- Home Manager statistics (from tool):
  - Total options: 4,857
  - Top categories (sample): programs ≈ 2,618 options; services ≈ 1,009; wayland ≈ 159; xsession ≈ 157; home ≈ 62
- How to verify and search:
  - Official Home Manager options (searchable): https://nix-community.github.io/home-manager/options.html
  - Repository (to check if a program has a module like programs.<name>): https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/search?q=programs.&type=code

How to find the exact details for “your package” (name not provided yet)
1) Find the attribute name and available versions across channels
- Web (quick):
  - Stable 25.11: https://search.nixos.org/packages?channel=25.11&query=<your-package>
  - Unstable: https://search.nixos.org/packages?channel=unstable&query=<your-package>
  - Previous stable 25.05: https://search.nixos.org/packages?channel=25.05&query=<your-package>
- CLI (flakes, precise and scriptable):
  - Find version on stable 25.11:
    nix eval --raw "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-25.11#legacyPackages.x86_64-linux.<attr>.version"
  - Find version on unstable:
    nix eval --raw "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-unstable#legacyPackages.x86_64-linux.<attr>.version"
  - If you don’t know the attribute name, first do:
    nix search nixpkgs <name-fragment>
    or use the NixOS search website above to get the exact attrpath.

2) Check if Home Manager has first-class support for it
- Look for programs.<name>.enable on the options site:
  - https://nix-community.github.io/home-manager/options.html#opt-programs.<name>.enable
- If it exists, you’ll get structured options under programs.<name>.* (e.g., settings, extraConfig).
- If it doesn’t, install it via Home Manager packages:
  - home.packages = with pkgs; [ <attr> ];
- To verify in repo:
  - https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/search?q=programs.%3Cname%3E.enable&type=code

3) Confirm the latest version vs. what’s in each channel
- Use the nix eval commands above for each channel.
- If you want the absolute latest from the nixpkgs repo regardless of channel, you can evaluate against a specific commit or nixpkgs/master, but that’s typically less stable than nixos-unstable or stable channels.
- You can cross-check the version shown on search.nixos.org for each channel.

Flakes: how to pin and stay stable (and where to verify)
- Flake inputs to pin:
  - nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-25.11"  (stable)
  - For unstable testing: "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-unstable"
- Home Manager input pinned to the matching release branch:
  - home-manager.url = "github:nix-community/home-manager/release-25.11"
  - Also add: home-manager.inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "nixpkgs"
- Minimal example (NixOS + HM, single host):
  flake.nix
  {
    inputs = {
      nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-25.11";
      home-manager.url = "github:nix-community/home-manager/release-25.11";
      home-manager.inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "nixpkgs";
    };
    outputs = { nixpkgs, home-manager, ... }: {
      nixosConfigurations.myhost = nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem {
        system = "x86_64-linux";
        modules = [
          ./configuration.nix
          home-manager.nixosModules.home-manager
          {
            home-manager.useGlobalPkgs = true;
            home-manager.useUserPackages = true;
            home-manager.users.yourUser = import ./home.nix;
          }
        ];
      };
    };
  }
- Verification and docs:
  - Flakes overview: https://nixos.wiki/wiki/Flakes
  - Home Manager with NixOS module: https://nix-community.github.io/home-manager/index.html#nixos-module
  - After editing inputs, lock your versions:
    nix flake update
    And inspect:
    nix flake metadata
- Note on flake search: our tool reported “Flake indices not found. Flake search may be temporarily unavailable.” Use search.nixos.org or direct nix eval as shown above.

Putting it all together (stable builds + finding “the latest”)
- For stable builds: use nixos-25.11 and the matching Home Manager release branch; pin them in your flake (see example) and commit flake.lock.
- To confirm the latest available version in each channel for your package:
  - Run nix eval --raw ... for nixos-25.11, 25.05, and nixos-unstable, and compare the version strings.
- If the package has a Home Manager module, prefer programs.<name>.* options for configuration; otherwise add it to home.packages.
- If you need a newer version than stable provides, you can:
  - Temporarily pull just that package from unstable via an overlay or a separate nixpkgs input in your flake, while keeping the rest pinned to stable.

