Abstract
Image captions serve as efficient surrogates for visual con-
tent in multimodal systems such as retrieval, recommenda-
tion, and multi-step agentic inference pipelines. Yet cur-
rent evaluation practices miss a fundamental question:Can
captions stand-in for images in real downstream tasks?We
propose a utility-based benchmark,CaptionQA, to eval-
uate model-generated captions, where caption quality is
measured by how well it supports downstream tasks. Cap-
tionQA is an extensible domain-dependent benchmark cov-
ering 4 domains–Natural, Document, E-commerce, and
Embodied AI–each with fine-grained taxonomies (25 top-
level and 69 subcategories) that identify useful informa-
tion for domain-specific tasks. CaptionQA builds 33...
