Abstract
Existing benchmarks for visual document retrieval (VDR) largely overlook non-English lan-
guages and the structural complexity of official publications. To address this gap, we introduce
SDS KoPub VDR, the first large-scale, public benchmark for retrieving and understanding Ko-
rean public documents. The benchmark is built upon 361 real-world documents, including 256
files under the KOGL Type 1 license and 105 from official legal portals, capturing complex vi-
sual elements like tables, charts, and multi-column layouts. To establish a reliable evaluation set,
we constructed 600 query-page-answer triples. These were initially generated...
