- Results: Strong lip-sync, visual quality, and natural multi-person interactivity; favorable trade-off between data cost and identity scalability.

5) SmallWorlds: Benchmarking Dynamics Understanding of World Models (cs.LG)
- Contribution: A controlled testbed (“SmallWorld”) to rigorously assess whether world models capture environment dynamics without relying on handcrafted rewards.
- Scope: Fully observable settings; evaluates RSSM, Transformer, Diffusion, Neural ODE across six domains.
- Findings: Insights on structure capture and long-horizon rollout degradation; identifies strengths/limitations and directions for better representation/dynamics modeling.

6) The Price of Progress: Algorithmic Efficiency and Falling AI Inference Costs (cs.LG; cs.AI; cs.CY)
- Data: Largest dataset of historical/current prices to run benchmarks (Artificial Analysis + Epoch AI).
- Findings: For frontier models on knowledge, reasoning, math, and software engineering, price for a given performance has fallen ~5×–10× per year. After controlling for hardware and competition (open models), algorithmic efficiency ≈3× per year.
- Recommendation: Evaluations should report and factor in benchmarking prices to reflect real-world impact.

