- CaptionQA: Is Your Caption as Useful as the Image Itself?
  - Addresses the gap between current caption evaluations and their actual utility as surrogates for images in multimodal systems (retrieval, recommendation, agentic pipelines).
  - Proposes an evaluation framework centered on the functional usefulness of captions relative to the source images.

- OmniRefiner: Reinforcement-Guided Local Diffusion Refinement
  - Targets reference-guided image generation’s difficulty preserving fine-grained details during refinement.
  - Introduces reinforcement-guided local diffusion refinement to better retain and transfer local visual details from references.

- Fast3Dcache: Training-free 3D Geometry Synthesis Acceleration
  - Speeds up computationally expensive iterative denoising in 3D diffusion-based shape generation.
  - Proposes a training-free caching mechanism to accelerate 3D geometry synthesis without retraining, aiming to preserve quality.

- Adversarial Flow Models
  - Unifies adversarial generative models and flow models into a single class.
  - Supports native one-step and multi-step generation; trained adversarially for flexible and efficient synthesis.

- Recognition of Abnormal Events in Surveillance Videos using Weakly Supervised Dual-Encoder Models
  - Tackles rare/diverse anomaly detection with only video-level labels.
  - Dual-backbone architecture fusing convolutional and transformer representations for robust weakly supervised abnormal event recognition.

- YOLO Meets Mixture-of-Experts: Adaptive Expert Routing for Robust Object Detection
  - Introduces a Mixture-of-Experts framework over multiple YOLOv9-T experts with adaptive routing.
  - Enables dynamic feature specialization for higher accuracy and robustness across conditions.

- Find the Leak, Fix the Split: Cluster-Based Method to Prevent Leakage in Video-Derived Datasets
  - Mitigates information leakage when splitting video-derived frames into train/val/test.
  - Clusters visually similar frames first, then splits, to avoid near-duplicate leakage and produce fairer evaluations.

- From Pixels to Feelings: Aligning MLLMs with Human Cognitive Perception of Images
  - Highlights MLLMs’ gap in modeling how images “feel” to humans (affective/cognitive perception), beyond object/scene recognition.
  - Proposes aligning MLLMs with human cognitive perception signals to better capture image-level affective understanding.

- RefineBench: Evaluating Refinement Capability of Language Models via Checklists
  - Asks whether LMs can self-refine their responses—central to many real-world interactions.
  - Introduces a checklist-based benchmark to systematically evaluate refinement capability, exposing shortcomings and guiding progress.

- World in a Frame: Understanding Culture Mixing as a New Challenge for Vision-Language Models
  - Defines “culture mixing” scenarios where culturally diverse elements co-occur in the same scene.
  - Examines LVLMs’ robustness on this new challenge and analyzes their behavior under mixed cultural contexts.

- Vision Bridge Transformer at Scale
  - Presents Vision Bridge Transformer (ViBT), a large-scale Brownian Bridge model for conditional generation.
