Goal
Evaluate whether model-generated captions can stand in for images in real downstream tasks by directly measuring their utility, not just their detail or overlap with references.

Key idea
Use multiple-choice QA that explicitly requires visual information, then ask a text-only LLM to answer using only the caption (QA-on-caption). Compare to QA-on-image performance to quantify the “utility gap.” This tests if captions preserve the image’s task-relevant information and if downstream LLMs can utilize it.

Scope and dataset
- Domains: 4 real-world domains with distinct needs
  - Natural, Document, E-commerce, Embodied AI
- Taxonomy: 2-level, domain-specific schemas
