Cluster and system design
- Node: 8× MI300X (192 GB HBM each) connected via InfinityFabric (xGMI), dual-socket Intel Xeon, 2 TB DDR5, 8× NVMe (3.2 TB each), one Pollara 400 Gbps NIC per GPU.
- Network topology: Two-level rails-only fabric (4 leaf switches, 4 spines per leaf), 30 servers per slice; trades some path diversity for cost/simplicity; requires parallelism/collectives to avoid cross-rail traffic.
- Two physically separate networks: Pollara fabric for training collectives; VPC network via Pensando DSC SmartNIC/DPUs (~200 Gbps to storage) for dataset IO/checkpoints/management to prevent interference with model comms.
- Head and storage nodes connected via separate interconnect to avoid contention.

